From: Haldexx <https://github.com/Haldexx>
Subject: [PATCH] common: add Gallery2 as the photo editor backend

The default gallery (Glimpse) has no built-in photo editor; its edit button fires an
ACTION_EDIT intent that had no in-ROM handler (only Google Photos from GApps). Add
Gallery2, whose manifest is already editor-only (FilterShowActivity/CropActivity for
ACTION_EDIT and CROP). Restores in-gallery editing (crop, filters, adjust) without
GApps. Verified on N920I: the editor opens and renders on Android 16.

---
 device-common.mk | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device-common.mk b/device-common.mk
--- a/device-common.mk
+++ b/device-common.mk
@@ -30,6 +30,10 @@
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 	AdvancedDisplay
 
+# Gallery editor backend for Glimpse (ACTION_EDIT: crop, filters, adjust)
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+	Gallery2
+
 # Atrace HAL
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 	android.hardware.atrace@1.0-service.universal7420
-- 
